## Data Model

```mermaid
erDiagram
    USER {
        ObjectId _id
        String phone UK
        String name
        String passwordHash
        String role "devotee | templeAdmin | superadmin"
        ObjectId assignedTemple FK "nullable"
    }
    TEMPLE {
        ObjectId _id
        String name
        String description
        String location
        String deity
        String image "emoji"
        String imageUrl
        String timings
        Array operatingHours "open/close HH:mm pairs"
        Boolean isActive
    }
    SLOT {
        ObjectId _id
        String date "YYYY-MM-DD"
        String startTime "HH:mm"
        String endTime "HH:mm"
        String label "A, B, C..."
        Number maxCapacity
        Number currentBooked
        Boolean isActive
        ObjectId templeId FK
    }
    BOOKING {
        ObjectId _id
        ObjectId user FK
        ObjectId slot FK
        String status "confirmed | cancelled"
        Date bookedAt
    }

    TEMPLE ||--o{ SLOT : "has many"
    SLOT ||--o{ BOOKING : "has many"
    USER ||--o{ BOOKING : "makes"
    USER }o--|| TEMPLE : "manages (if templeAdmin)"
```

> **Key relationships:** A Temple has many 15-min Slots. A User books a Slot to create a Booking. A templeAdmin user is assigned exactly one Temple.

---

## Authentication & Authorization (RBAC)

### Three Roles

| Role | Scope |
|---|---|
| **`devotee`** | Browse temples, view slots, create bookings, see own bookings |
| **`templeAdmin`** | All devotee abilities + manage their assigned temple's slots, view temple bookings, temple dashboard stats |
| **`superadmin`** | Full system access — CRUD all users/temples/slots, view all bookings, global stats, assign roles |

### Auth Flow

1. **Register** → `POST /api/auth/register` — creates user with `devotee` role, returns JWT (7-day expiry)
2. **Login** → `POST /api/auth/login` — verifies phone + password, returns JWT
3. **Protected routes** use the [protect](file:///f:/project/darshaneasebackend/src/middlewares/auth.middleware.ts#9-27) middleware (extracts JWT from `Authorization: Bearer <token>`)
4. **Role-gated routes** stack [requireRole('superadmin')](file:///f:/project/darshaneasebackend/src/middlewares/auth.middleware.ts#28-46) or [requireRole('templeAdmin')](file:///f:/project/darshaneasebackend/src/middlewares/auth.middleware.ts#28-46) on top of [protect](file:///f:/project/darshaneasebackend/src/middlewares/auth.middleware.ts#9-27)

