## Key Design Patterns

1. **Service Layer Separation** — Business logic (`auth.service`, `booking.service`) is decoupled from HTTP handling in controllers. This makes logic reusable (e.g., `bookingService.createBooking` is used by both the direct booking route *and* the payment simulation route).

2. **Atomic Booking Counter** — [booking.service.ts](file:///f:/project/darshaneasebackend/src/services/booking.service.ts) uses Mongoose `$inc` to atomically increment `currentBooked` on the slot, preventing double-booking under concurrent requests.

3. **Zod Env Validation** — The server fails-fast at startup if required environment variables (`MONGODB_URI`, `JWT_SECRET`) are missing or invalid.

4. **Populate Chains** — Booking queries use deep population (`booking → slot → temple`) to deliver denormalized responses.

5. **Ownership Scoping** — Temple admins can only access resources belonging to their `assignedTemple`, enforced via the [getAssignedTemple()](file:///f:/project/darshaneasebackend/src/controllers/templeAdmin.controller.ts#10-26) helper in every templeAdmin controller method.

---

## What's Working Well ✅

- Clean layered architecture (routes → controllers → services → models)
- RBAC with middleware composition is simple and effective
- Multi-temple support with per-temple slot management
- Atomic booking counter prevents overbooking
- Seed scripts make development and demo setup fast
- Zod validates critical env vars at startup

---

## Current Limitations & Gaps ⚠️

| Area | Issue |
|---|---|
| **Payment** | Simulated only (2s delay + fake ID). No real gateway. |
| **No Booking Cancellation API** | Status field exists (`confirmed`, `cancelled`) but no cancel endpoint |
| **No Pagination** | All list endpoints return full result sets—will become slow at scale |
| **No Rate Limiting** | Open to brute-force login and spam requests |
| **No Input Validation** | Controllers do manual `!field` checks; no Zod on request bodies |
| **No Email/SMS** | No notifications for booking confirmations |
| **No Queue System** | No live queue/crowd estimation |
| **No Tests** | Zero unit or integration tests |
| **Hard Deletion** | Users and temples are hard-deleted, not soft-deleted |
| **No Logging** | No structured logging (e.g., Winston, Pino) |
| **No Error Handling Middleware** | Each controller catches its own errors; no global handler |

---

## 🚀 Future Scope

### Phase 1 — Production Hardening

| Feature | Details |
|---|---|
| **Real Payment Gateway** | Integrate Razorpay or PhonePe. Add [Payment](file:///f:/project/darshaneasebackend/src/controllers/payment.controller.ts#13-56) model to track transactions. Use webhook callbacks for confirmation. |
| **Booking Cancellation & Refund** | `PATCH /api/bookings/:id/cancel` with `$inc: { currentBooked: -1 }` on the slot and optional refund trigger. |
| **Request Validation** | Use Zod schemas as Express middleware on every route to validate and sanitize request bodies/params/queries. |
| **Global Error Handler** | Central [(err, req, res, next)](file:///f:/project/darshaneasebackend/src/services/auth.service.ts#44-66) middleware with structured error codes and stack traces in development. |
| **Rate Limiting** | `express-rate-limit` on auth endpoints (5 req/min) and public APIs. |
| **Structured Logging** | Pino or Winston with request correlation IDs. |
| **Pagination & Filtering** | Implement cursor-based or offset pagination on all list endpoints. |
| **Automated Testing** | Unit tests for services, integration tests for routes (Jest + Supertest). |

### Phase 2 — Feature Expansion

| Feature | Details |
|---|---|
| **Live Queue / Crowd Status** | Real-time crowd estimation using WebSockets (`socket.io`). Display current wait time and crowd density per slot. |
| **QR Code Check-in** | Generate QR codes on booking confirmation. Temple admin scans to mark attendance. |
| **Push Notifications** | Firebase Cloud Messaging for booking reminders, slot availability alerts. |
| **Email / SMS Confirmations** | Integrate Nodemailer + Twilio for booking receipts and OTP-based auth. |
| **OTP-Based Login** | Replace password auth with phone OTP for devotees; keep password for admins. |
| **Donation Module** | Online donations per-temple with receipt generation. |
| **Special Darshan (VIP)** | Premium slot tiers with different pricing and faster entry. |
| **Multi-Language Support** | `i18n` middleware for Hindi, Tamil, Telugu, etc. |

### Phase 3 — Scale & Intelligence

| Feature | Details |
|---|---|
| **Caching** | Redis for frequently accessed temple lists, slot availability. |
| **CDN for Images** | Cloudinary integration (already in [package.json](file:///f:/project/darshaneasebackend/package.json)) for temple images with transformations. |
| **Analytics Dashboard** | Aggregate booking trends, peak hours, popular temples using MongoDB aggregation pipelines. |
| **ML-Based Crowd Prediction** | Use historical booking data to predict peak times and recommend less busy slots. |
| **Microservices Split** | Extract booking, payment, and notifications into separate services as traffic grows. |
| **API Versioning** | Version routes (`/api/v1/`, `/api/v2/`) for backward compatibility. |
| **CI/CD Pipeline** | GitHub Actions for lint, test, build, and deploy to AWS/Vercel. |
| **Container & Orchestration** | Docker + Kubernetes for horizontal scaling and zero-downtime deployments. |

---

> **Summary:** The DarshanEase backend is a well-structured, TypeScript + Express + MongoDB REST API with a 3-tier RBAC system supporting devotees, temple admins, and a superadmin. It handles multi-temple darshan slot booking with atomic capacity management. The current system is a solid MVP — the biggest next steps are integrating a real payment gateway, adding automated tests, improving input validation, and building out the live queue status feature.
